        {
          "id": "7501600288085078019",
          "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7501600288085078019",
          "title": "A flaky test is useful only when the failure leaves enough evidence to classify it.\nIn my Playwright work, stability comes from three layers: user-facing locators, controlled test data, and API or trace evidence behind the UI result. That makes it possible to separate an application defect from timing, authentication, environment, or test-code problems before anyone reaches for rerun.\nA test suite should reduce debugging time, not create another system to debug.\n#Playwright #QualityEngineering #TestAutomation #SoftwareTesting",
