        {
          "id": "7500190661334249473",
          "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7500190661334249473",
          "title": "I’ve learned to treat flaky tests as a signal, not just an annoyance.\n\nA test that fails intermittently may be exposing timing assumptions, shared state, unstable data, or a real race condition. Rerunning it until it passes hides the risk and weakens trust in the suite.\n\nThe better question is: what changed between the passing and failing runs?\n\nI’m curious where others draw the line between quarantine and investigation. Push back if your approach differs.",
