        {
          "id": "7492876837518364672",
          "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7492876837518364672",
          "title": "🚀 Article 2 - Five Common Reasons Selenium Tests Become Flaky — And How to Fix Them — \nOne of the biggest challenges I’ve faced while working with Selenium automation is flaky tests — tests that pass sometimes, fail sometimes, and leave you wondering what actually went wrong. 😅\nSo, for my second blog article, I’ve covered:\n🔹 5 common reasons Selenium tests become flaky\n🔹 Why time.sleep() can cause problems\n🔹 Handling dynamic web elements with explicit waits\n🔹 Building stable locators\n🔹 Managing test data\n🔹 Avoiding test dependencies\n🔹 Practical ways to make Selenium tests more reliable\n🎯 The goal is simple: write automation that you can actually trust.\nIf you’re working with Selenium, Python, PyTest, or QA Automation, I hope you find it useful.\n👉 I’d love to hear your experiences too — what has been the biggest cause of flaky tests in your automation projects?\n#Selenium #Python #PyTest #TestAutomation #QA #SoftwareTesting #AutomationTesting #SeleniumWebDriver",
