        {
          "id": "7500106623722475520",
          "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7500106623722475520",
          "title": "A test fails. You rerun it and it passes. Was there a defect? Was the test updated incorrectly? Or did the result change for no apparent reason?\n\nThat last case is flakiness: an automated test producing inconsistent results across executions on the same build, environment and inputs.\n\nThe issue is not one occasional false failure. When pass rates oscillate, every failure must be triaged twice: first to establish whether it is real, then to fix it if it is. The suite becomes harder to trust and harder to read.\n\nRead the blog to understand why flaky tests are a strategic problem, not just a tactical annoyance: https://lnkd.in/es8uGkjC\n\n#TestAutomation #SoftwareTesting #QualityAssurance",
