        {
          "id": "7501845797064556544",
          "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7501845797064556544",
          "title": "Most flaky tests aren't flaky.\n\nThey're timing bugs wearing a costume.\n\nWhen a suite \"randomly\" fails, the easy move is to retry until green. The useful move is to ask: what race did we paper over? What shared state leaked? What assumption about the network died under real traffic?\n\nRetries hide the problem. They don't fix it.\n\nNext time a test flakes twice in a week, treat it like a production incident — not a CI annoyance.\n\n#QA #SoftwareTesting #SDET #QualityEngineering #TestAutomation\n\n[AUTOMATED POST]",
