        {
          "id": "7501701620469112832",
          "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7501701620469112832",
          "title": "Flaky tests erode trust faster than missing tests do. Once a test suite cries wolf enough times, engineers stop reading the red and start re-running until it goes green. At that point the suite is providing less signal than no suite at all, just more ceremony around ignoring it.\n\nFixing flakiness is unglamorous work. It rarely gets prioritized on its own, only after someone gets burned by a real bug that a flaky test also happened to be flagging that week.\n\nTreat flaky as a bug in the test, not a fact of life.\n\n#BuildInPublic #SoftwareTesting #QA #TestAutomation",
